WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:08.549
This is the other way to connect Slack. A webhook is a private web address that posts into one specific channel. You make one for each channel.

00:00:08.749 --> 00:00:14.219
Open your Slack app. In the left menu choose Incoming Webhooks, and switch it on.

00:00:14.419 --> 00:00:20.721
Press Add New Webhook to Workspace. Choose the channel you want reports to land in, and press Allow.

00:00:20.921 --> 00:00:28.418
Slack gives you a Webhook URL. Press Copy. Treat it like a password, because anyone who has it can post in that channel.

00:00:28.618 --> 00:00:38.355
On the settings page, open Prefer webhooks, and paste the address into the matching box. Repeat for each channel, press Save Slack, then Send test messages.

00:00:38.555 --> 00:00:43.726
That is it. One webhook for each channel, and your reports will start arriving.
